   146                              <1> ; PrintAt: DH=row DL=col BL=colour SI=zero-terminated string.
   147                              <1> ; Draws the 8x8 ROM font straight into mode 13h video memory on the
   148                              <1> ; 40x25 character grid.  The cell background comes from [TextBg]:
   149                              <1> ; 0FFh = the sidebar gradient behind the cell, anything else = that
   150                              <1> ; solid colour (so text sits cleanly on dialogs and panels instead of
   151                              <1> ; on black BIOS boxes).  Text is clipped at column 40 - it never wraps
   152                              <1> ; onto the next row or scrolls the screen like BIOS teletype output.
